{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Before building one, we need vocabulary precise enough to avoid the confusion that sinks most people working with grids."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Dimensions"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "The **number of dimensions** is how many indices you need to pinpoint one value."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**One dimension** — `scores[i]`. A line. One index.",
        "**Two dimensions** — `grid[r][c]`. A rectangle. Two indices.",
        "**Three dimensions** — `cube[x][y][z]`. A box. Three indices."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Two dimensions covers almost everything you will meet in practice, so that is where we will stay."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Rows and columns"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "A 2D array has a **shape**, written rows x columns. A 3 x 4 grid has 3 rows and 4 columns, for 12 cells in total."
    },
